  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The frame path",
      "items": [
        "Keys travel down the stack; frames come back up a subscription, never an import.",
        "StateFlow drops an unchanged frame, so an idle tick never touches curses."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Layers",
      "items": [
        "ui is the only package that imports curses; presentation holds the domain too.",
        "util is plumbing any layer may use, and there is no data layer at all."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "One thread",
      "items": [
        "curses is not thread-safe, so the clock is polled by the loop, never fired by a timer.",
        "Nothing outlives the process: no files, no network, no database."
      ]
    }
  ]
